---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Samuel Sorial is a senior backend developer focused on distributed systems, databases, and system design.">
  <article class="article shell about-shell">
    <header class="about-intro">
      <span class="section-kicker">About me</span>
      <h1>Backend engineer,<br /><span>systems thinker.</span></h1>
      <p class="about-lead">I’m Samuel Sorial, a Senior Backend Developer at Cloud Imperium Games. I build backend systems using distributed-systems concepts and practical system-design principles.</p>
      <a class="profile-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/samuel-sorial/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener noreferrer">
        View my LinkedIn profile
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 17 17 7M8 7h9v9" /></svg>
      </a>
    </header>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <section class="about-card">
        <span class="card-index">01</span>
        <h2>What I work on</h2>
        <p>Backend development, distributed systems, databases, and the engineering decisions that make software reliable as it grows.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="about-card">
        <span class="card-index">02</span>
        <h2>How I learn</h2>
        <p>I enjoy moving between languages and frameworks, using each one as a different tool for understanding and solving a problem.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="about-card about-card-wide">
        <span class="card-index">03</span>
        <h2>Why this blog exists</h2>
        <p>This is my public technical notebook: a place to work through new concepts, document what I learn, and leave behind explanations I can return to later.</p>
        <div class="skill-list" aria-label="Core topics">
          <span>Node.js</span><span>Databases</span><span>Distributed systems</span><span>System design</span>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
